  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - INDONESIA: JAKARTA AIR QUALITY MONITORING AND IMPROVEMENT NETWORK CHANGE ACTIVITY FROM FEASIBILITY STUDY GRANT TO DIRECT CONTRACT TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE, through Sullivan Environmental Consulting, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The $291,000 direct contract technical assistance (initially a $291,000 feasibility study grant) aims to help implement an Air Quality Monitoring and Improvement Project overseen by Daerah Khusu Ibukota Jakarta (DKI Jakarta), the provincial government of Jakarta, Indonesia. The assistance determines the appropriate equipment, configuration, and monitoring locations for an air quality monitoring network project in the greater Jakarta region. The project to be implemented would entail the installation and operation of fifteen new stationary air quality monitoring stations and one mobile air quality monitoring unit. This network of stations will assess air pollution impacts from the transportation, domestic, and industrial sectors. This information will guide the policy decision for air quality management of the Jakarta provincial government, DKI Jakarta.</narrative>
  </description>
